<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sæberht of Essex</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 616</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Also known as Saeberht of Essex</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sæberht was king of the East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxons</a> from about 604 until about 616 and the first Christian king of Essex. A nephew of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aethelberht-of-kent">Æthelberht of Kent</a>, he accepted baptism and allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mellitus">Mellitus</a> to establish a bishopric in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>, but his sons returned to paganism after his death. A rich burial found at Prittlewell in 2003 may be his.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saeberht-of-essex.jpg" alt="Sæberht of Essex" width="320" height="301" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Speed · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sebert_-_John_Speed.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
